1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
AI agents can recommend anything. TasteProof makes them show what the evidence actually supports.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:15,000
First, consent. On the live site, nothing reaches Qloo until a reviewer approves.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Two anchors, one city, three AI-proposed venues. The reviewer approves resolving them through Qloo Search.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Qloo answers with real candidates. Both names are ambiguous, so the reviewer picks the exact entities.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Confirmed anchors, city and shortlist on screen. The reviewer approves one combined Insights check.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
The verdicts: OBSERVED means an exact match in this result set. REVIEW means look closer.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,500
NOT OBSERVED means absent from these results. Never proof a place doesn't exist.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,500
Same verification, callable by another AI agent. Standard MCP — not a mock.

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Tools list, capabilities, then verify shortlist with an owner-minted approval. Three provider calls.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
One observed, one review, one not observed — computed from real Qloo IDs.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The uncertain venue gets one bounded follow-up: investigate gap.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Separate Search evidence, reported alongside. The original REVIEW verdict never changes.

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
A forged approval is rejected with zero provider calls. The browser never holds tokens.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Every run ends with a receipt: IDs, counts, and explicit limits.

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Affinity is a ranking signal, never a match percentage. Hours and prices are never verified.

16
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Try it live: no account, no keys. Reviewers verify; developers call POST /api/mcp.

17
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:04,000
TasteProof: receipts, not vibes.
